{"name":"July Ruby","hex":"#773b4a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ruby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A clear, deep, red variety of corundum, valued as a precious stone.","A deep red colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep, red color; ruby-red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruby"}],"entries":[{"title":"July","blocks":[{"text":"July is the seventh month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 31 days. It was named by the Roman Senate in honour of Roman general and statesman Julius Caesar in 44 B.C., being the month of his birth. Before then it was called Quintilis, being the fifth month of the calendar that started with March."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/July","wikidata":"Q121"},{"title":"Ruby","blocks":[{"text":"Ruby is a pinkish-red to blood-red-colored gemstone, a variety of the mineral corundum, consisting of aluminium oxide (α-Al2O3). Ruby is one of the most popular traditional jewelry gems and is very durable. Other varieties of gem-quality corundum are called sapphires, and rubies are also sometimes referred to as \"red sapphires\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Corundum-215330.jpg/330px-Corundum-215330.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruby","wikidata":"Q43088"},{"title":"Ruby (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Ruby is a color that is a representation of the color of the cut and polished ruby gemstone and is a shade of red or pink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Ruby_gem.JPG/330px-Ruby_gem.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruby_(color)","wikidata":"Q3446513"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Baker%27s_Larkspur_%285933879987%29.jpg/500px-Baker%27s_Larkspur_%285933879987%29.jpg?utm